<div id="step-1">
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-center pt-0 mt-0">
        <div class="col-xs-12 col-sm-12 col-md-12 col-lg-12 ">
            <div class="panel border-theme-color customPanel">
                <div class="panel-heading bg-theme-color text-center d-flex justify-content-center pl-2 pr-2">
                    Step 1/7<span class="d-none d-sm-block"> - Introduction</span>
                </div>
                <div class="panel-body pb-2">
                    <div id="divIntroduction">
                        <div class="row">
                            <div class="col-md-12">
                                <p>
                                    AMREF University financial aid awards are designed to help students who are financially
                                    challenged in meeting their school fees. Successful applicants will be required to work at least ten
                                    hours per week throughout the 34 weeks of the regular academic year irrespective of the amount of
                                    the scholarship. The applicant is hereby notified that the amount of the work-study aid is based on
                                    the actual hours worked.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    Application for AMREF University financial aid is open to all students, however, the number of
                                    awards given are constrained by various limitations including but not limited to the amount of
                                    funds available for distribution. Due to such and other limitations not mentioned herein, not all
                                    students who apply will receive the award. All applicants are advised to save or print a copy of the
                                    application form should they need to refer to it. Financial Aid is applied on an annual basis. All
                                    successful applicants will be required to apply for it again if they wish to be considered in
                                    subsequent years.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    Preference in allocating financial aid grants will be given to those who:
                                    <ol>
                                        <li>Are enrolled full-time (or at least 15credit hours).</li>
                                        <li>Possess above average academic achievement (at least 2.5 cum GPA).</li>
                                        <li>
                                            Demonstrate a lifestyle consistent with the University’s mission and vision in all areas of
                                            their student life.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>Have a demonstrated financial need.</li>
                                        <li>Are closer to completing their program of study.</li>
                                        <li>Exhibit a strong Christian character and involvement.</li>
                                        <li>
                                            To those students who, in the past one year have NOT been charged and convicted of
                                            misconduct.
                                        </li>
                                    </ol>
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    For this application to be considered, the following requirements must be met:
                                    <ol>
                                        <li>
                                            Application for loan or bursary from the Higher Education Loans Board (HELB), as well as
                                            County Government bursary or Constituency Development Funds (CDF) (for Kenyan
                                            citizens) or equivalent sources from your country (if you are an international student). You
                                            should attach copies of your application to this form irrespective of whether you received
                                            the assistance or not.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            This form must be filled in full. Any questions not relevant to the applicant should be filled
                                            with the “N/A” sign. Incomplete forms or those containing false information will be
                                            rejected.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            All responses should be given in the English language with correct spelling, grammar, and
                                            punctuation.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            All responses should be filled in the spaces provided and in the manner prescribed. The
                                            student’s parent, guardian, or sponsor should complete all parts that are relevant to them.
                                        </li>
                                        <li>
                                            The completely filled form must be submitted to the Financial Aid Office with supporting
                                            documents on or before 31st January each year. Late applications will not be considered.
                                        </li>
                                    </ol>
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
